   "k": "5hat4o",
   "en": "The Shanxi clique was one of several military factions that split off from the Beiyang Army during China's warlord era after the Xinhai Revolution in 1911. The clique was led by General Yan Xishan, which preferred neutrality in the wars between various warring factions in ⟦0⟧, Yan was in favour of the use of westernization to preserve Chinese tradition, he also implemented various economical and social reforms, earning his nickname of the ⟦1⟧. In 1928 Chiang Kai-shek rises through power in the Kuomintang and launches the Northern Expedition, defeating various warlords and partially unifying China. In an attempt to restore the balance of power, Yan Xishan together with several other warlords (specifically ⟦2⟧, Beyiang Clique and the ⟦3⟧) launched the Central Plains War but were defeated. The clique joined the Chinese United Front, and they were significantly weakened by the Japanese invasion which occupied most of their base province. After the war, Yan Xishan was unable to defend his province which fell to the Communists in 1949, forcing him to escape to Taiwan with the rest of the Kuomintang.",
